    "syns": [
      {
        "pl": "synonyms",
        "pt": [
          [
            "text",
            "{sc}cool{/sc} {sc}composed{/sc} {sc}collected{/sc} {sc}unruffled{/sc} {sc}imperturbable{/sc} {sc}nonchalant{/sc} mean free from agitation or excitement. {sc}cool{/sc} may imply calmness, deliberateness, or dispassionateness. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "kept a {it}cool{/it} head"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "text",
            " {sc}composed{/sc} implies freedom from agitation as a result of self-discipline or a sedate disposition. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "the {it}composed{/it} pianist gave a flawless concert"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "text",
            " {sc}collected{/sc} implies a concentration of mind that eliminates distractions especially in moments of crisis. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "the nurse stayed calm and {it}collected{/it}"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "text",
            " {sc}unruffled{/sc} suggests apparent serenity and poise in the face of setbacks or in the midst of excitement. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "harried but {it}unruffled{/it}"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "text",
            " {sc}imperturbable{/sc} implies coolness or assurance even under severe provocation. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "the speaker remained {it}imperturbable{/it} despite the heckling"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "text",
            " {sc}nonchalant{/sc} stresses an easy coolness of manner or casualness that suggests indifference or unconcern. "
          ],
          [
            "vis",
            [
              {
                "t": "a {it}nonchalant{/it} driver"
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "et": [
      [
        "text",
        "Middle English {it}col,{/it} going back to Old English {it}cōl,{/it} going back to West Germanic {it}*kōlu-{/it} (whence also Middle Dutch {it}coele{/it} \"moderately cold\" and, from a variant {it}*kōlja-,{/it} Old High German {it}kuoli{/it}), lengthened-grade derivative from the base of {it}*kalan-{/it} \"to be cold\" {ma}{mat|cold:1|}{/ma}"
      ]
